  "cleanText": "Solution home \n\t\tTime and Fees\n\t\tTime and Fees\n\n### Time and Fees - Settings\n\n\t\t\tPrint\n\n\tModified on: Wed, 10 Apr, 2024 at  1:19 PM\n\n\t\tIntroduction to Time and Fees Module\n\nTime and Fees is designed to Manage the Jobs and Tasks in a estimated Time and Fees\n\nGetting Started\n\nSettings\n\nIn the Settings Menu, we have the 5 sections below:\n\nMy Business\n\nPreferences\n\nInvoices\n\nEstimates\n\nTemplates\n\nIntegrations\n\nNavigation: Settings>My Business \n\nhttps://timeandfees.capium.com/settings/mybusiness\n\nIn this section, the company details  will be available and the  admin user will  be able to amend or update the details of the company\n\nCompany Name\n\nCompany Number\n\nVAT Number\n\nAddress\n\nContact\n\nUpload logo\n\n Preferences:\n\nNavigation: Settings> Preferences\n\nhttps://timeandfees.capium.com/settings/preferences\n\nIn this section, the admin can choose the preferences based on the requirement\n\n    The information below can be updated in the Preferences section by the Admin user\n\nStart Week on\n\nDefault Capacity Hours per week\n\nTimesheet Due on\n\nTimesheet Reminder\n\nApproval Reminder \n\nTime Format\n\nTime Mode\n\nDemo Data\n\nNavigation: Settings> Demo Data\n\nhttps://timeandfees.capium.com/settings/demodata\n\nIn this section  you have the demo information across the module,  the admin user can view data from one section to another section while you're in demo mode. \n\nInvoices\n\nNavigation: Settings>> Invoices\n\nhttps://timeandfees.capium.com/settings/invoice\n\nIn Invoices the admin can choose the preferences for Invoices. It includes the \n\nInvoice ID generation type: In invoice generation id there are 2 option to select either Autogenerate or Add Manually \n\nPayment Method\n\nPayment Due Term \n\nVAT details\n\nSending Recurring invoices option\n\nFooter\n\nNavigate> Settings> Invoices\n\nUnder this section the admin can select the table columns as the columns and its naming that you select  will be applied to all the 'Fees' sections by default. If you wish to change any particular invoice or recurring invoice or estimate fields, you can do that from respective pages at detailed grid\n\nEstimates:\n\n Navigation: Settings> Estimates\n\nhttps://timeandfees.capium.com/settings/estimate\n\nIn this section, the admin can select the Estimate ID generation type (Autogenerate or Add Manually) and Prefix and suffix of Estimate of Fees for the clients along with the Footer\n\n Templates\n\nNavigation: Settings> Templates\n\nhttps://timeandfees.capium.com/settings/template\n\nIn this section, the Capium will be providing the default templates for the below-mentioned sections. The  user can make the changes and use the available Tags accordingly\n\nInvoices\n\nPayments\n\nReminders\n\nEstimates\n\nTimesheets\n\nExpense\n\nSignature\n\nNavigation: Settings>> Templates>>Signature for all emails\n\nIntegrations:\n\n Navigation:  Settings>> Integrations\n\nhttps://timeandfees.capium.com/settings/integration\n\nIn this Section, the system will show that the Time & Fee module has been integrated with different applications\n\n   The system has been integrated with the following options:\n\n    Email: The user can use the Capium Emails for Time and Fee or use Gmail or Outlook based on the requirement\n\nIf you encounter any issues or require further assistance, don't hesitate to reach out to your Onboarding Manager.\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tDid you find it helpful?\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tYes\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tNo\n\nSend feedback\tSorry we couldn't be helpful. Help us improve this article with your feedback.",
